# A notification's life over C's own table: the first CLEAR is not sent; WARNING, CRITICAL and the CLEAR after them
# are. Each pass leaves its command running (the entry and its row with the run and in-progress marks), and the
# wait that follows gives the entry its exit code in memory only.
database real
auto-wait 0
rules tests/corpus/notify/plain.conf
chart loop.n loop.n_name loop.notify disks things 1
label loop.n kind ssd
var loop.n v 10
clock 0
pass 0
wait
var loop.n v 70
clock 1
pass 1
clock 2
wait
var loop.n v 95
clock 3
pass 3
wait
var loop.n v 10
clock 4
pass 4
wait
clock 5
pass 5
clock 6
alarm-log 0
